course: dictionary
lesson: 1271
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words wear more than one coat. Business can mean a company or shop, the work of buying and selling, a private matter, or an affair. Context tells you which meaning you need. In «the small business sells cakes on Saturdays», business means a shop, because it sells things.
explain: Look at the words around it. In «It's no business of mine», the speaker is saying the matter does not concern them, so business means a private matter. «Mind your own business» means do not poke into other people's affairs. Leo guesses business is always about money, but the clues show it is not.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If «a strange business» means a strange affair, does the sentence still make sense? Yes, so you have found the right meaning. If it does not fit, try another meaning from the list.
fact: Business is a noun, and its plural is businesses.
fact: «Business» can mean a company, shop or firm that makes or sells things to earn money.
fact: «Business» can mean the work of buying, selling and making money.
fact: «Your business» means something that concerns only you.
fact: «A strange business» means a strange affair or matter.
exercise: «Ransomware has stopped hospitals, schools and businesses.» What are businesses here? | *Companies and shops that make or sell things | Places where people wash clothes | Lessons where children add up numbers | Trips that parents go on
exercise: «It's no business of mine.» What does business mean here? | A sum of money earned | A trip for work | *A matter that does not concern me | A shop that sells cakes
exercise: Ella's dad says, «Mind your own business.» What does he mean? | Ask the shopkeeper for a discount | *Do not poke into other people's affairs | Count the money in your purse | Go and buy a new business
test: In maths, pupils run a small business selling cakes to work out cost, price and profit. What does business mean here? | A private matter that only you should know about | A trip to a far-off town | *A company that makes and sells things to earn money | A strange affair with no clear reason
test: Which phrase means something is not your concern? | *It's none of your business | Business as usual | Small business | Run a business
exam: Which meaning of business fits best in «Toad lost all his money from his washing business»? | A matter that concerns only Toad | Mind your own business | *A company that makes or sells things to earn money | A strange affair
